The board file makes the SoC's USB controller a gadget as well as a host, which the kernel's
host-only driver reports as a configuration mismatch at every boot, and has the SD driver read a
write-protect switch that microSD slots lack. Its DMA ranges list the memory alone, and the Pi's SD
driver looks up the SD host's data register in them, so they list the peripherals too. A later
definition of a node overrides an earlier one.

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2835-rpi-zero.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm2835-rpi-zero.dts
@@ -117,3 +117,19 @@
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart0_gpio14>;
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+// lfs: overrides of the board file
+&usb {
+	dr_mode = "host";
+};
+
+&sdhost {
+	disable-wp;
+};
+
+/ {
+	soc {
+		dma-ranges = <0x40000000 0x00000000 0x20000000>,
+			     <0x7e000000 0x20000000 0x02000000>;
+	};
+};
